**What shipped**

- New published module [yang/clojure/prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc): `clj` runtime module at the §8.10 call address, with `clj/run-main`, plus task-local `clj/define-global!` and `clj/global-get` over `clj.rt/globals`.
- Linked lowering in [yang/clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc): reader as parser, and `lower-unit` published through the runtime globals so donor definitions discharge at link time. No calls were rewritten and no foreign `:code` was extracted.
- Foreign admission in the same compiler file: cell-backed callables are now read structurally through their cell contents. Forged source maps still need the existing witness, so admission was not weakened to “any map with an entry.”
- JS classification in [yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc): an admitted non-cell callable (a clojure descriptor or bound method) now has kind `:function` instead of falling through to `:number`.
- Profile and registry wiring in [yang/call/conformance.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/call/conformance.clj): full `:clojure` profile, donor publication over the admitted `kind`/`portable` registry, and a pinned `yang.call` requirement for qualified convention reads.
- Matrix legs in [yang/cross_lang_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj): named skip replaced by clojure→typescript and typescript→clojure same-cell legs. Integer crossing uses JS BigInt spelling (`20n`/`1n`), which is the same bare-int value Clojure uses.

